  "summary": "South San Francisco approved a two-year, ~$120,000/year contract with Flock Safety to expand its ALPR program from 28 to 44 cameras, and launched a drone program for police and fire. Police Chief Scott Campbell credited the ALPRs with 555 incidents and 147 arrests since 2022, while the article notes broader concerns about ALPR data-sharing with ICE and federal agencies.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Since the program's inception, the police department has documented 555 Flock-related incidents that have resulted in 147 arrests and dozens of cases being sent to the District Attorney's Office for arrest warrants and prosecution",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "more than 70 departments throughout California have been found to violate those rules, according to an investigation from the nonprofit Electronic Frontier Foundation",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "Councilmembers unanimously approved the expansion of the ALPR program.",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    }
  ],
